  "notes": {
    "js-extension-alias": "`@/lib/session.js` names a file that does not exist: under moduleResolution bundler/node16 TypeScript maps a `.js` specifier to the `.ts` source, so the target is src/lib/session.ts. The `@/*` alias comes from tsconfig.app.json, reached only through tsconfig.json `references` (Vite layout); tsconfig.json itself has no compilerOptions. tsconfig.app.json is JSONC (comment + trailing comma).",
    "js-extension-relative": "`./http.js` resolves to src/api/http.ts (same .js -> .ts mapping, relative form).",
    "js-imports-ts": "helpers.js is plain JS in an allowJs project; its extensionless `./storage` import resolves to storage.ts.",
    "namespace-import": "`import * as http from './http'` then `http.put()` / `http.get()` bind to the exported functions of http.ts.",
    "profile-save": "Profile.tsx imports `save` from `../api/users`; src/lib/helpers.js also exports a `save` and UserRepo has a `save` method. Only api/users.ts is bound.",
    "barrel": "`fetchPosts` imported from the `../api` barrel (src/api/index.ts) is defined in src/api/posts.ts; the call target is the defining file, the barrel itself defines nothing. The IMPORTS edge goes to the barrel file the specifier names.",
    "barrel-namespace": "`import * as api from '@/api'`; `api.fetchUser` comes through `export * from './users'`.",
    "renamed-import": "`import { save as saveDraft } from '../lib/helpers.js'`: the call site says saveDraft, the callee is the function `save` in helpers.js (a real .js file this time).",
    "new-typed-local": "`const svc = new UserService(...)`, so `svc.rename` is UserService.rename. Constructor invocations (`new X()`) are not listed as calls.",
    "ctor-param-properties": "`constructor(private repo: UserRepo, private readonly log: Logger) {}` declares fields repo/log; `this.repo.find` / `this.repo.save` / `this.repo.all` bind to UserRepo, `this.log.info` to Logger. `this.repo.save` must not go to api/users.ts or helpers.js.",
    "script-globals": "public/legacy.js and public/analytics.js are classic scripts (no import/export) loaded by index.html, so their top-level functions share the global scope. `formatDate` binds to legacy.js's own declaration, not to the module export in src/lib/text.ts; `trackEvent` binds to analytics.js. The `initLegacy` reference passed to addEventListener is not a call.",
    "alias-paths": "`@/lib/text` -> src/lib/text.ts via `paths` in tsconfig.app.json (relative to its baseUrl `.`).",
    "external-package": "react / react-dom are bare specifiers with no alias: external, no repo target.",
    "self-name-builtin": "A built-in method (Storage.getItem, Array.find, console.info) called from a repo method of the same name: must not become a self-loop.",
    "lodash": "`_.capitalize` is lodash, not src/lib/text.ts capitalize.",
    "type-only": "`import type` is erased at runtime but is still a source import of that file.",
    "alias": "Specifier resolved through the `@/*` path alias.",
    "re-export": "`export ... from` lines are imports of the re-exported file.",
    "scope": "JSX element usage (`<Profile />`, `<App />`) is a value reference, not a call, and is not listed. Calls inside anonymous arrows (onChange handler, Array.find predicate) are not listed. vite.config.ts only makes a module-level external call. index.html is not source."
  }
}
